<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Calchas</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Calchas is a seer of Greek mythology who served the Greek army in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/trojan-war">Trojan War</a>, demanding the sacrifice of Iphigenia and explaining the plague sent by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/apollo">Apollo</a> in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iliad">Iliad</a>. Later legends said that after the war he wandered with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mopsus">Mopsus</a> and other heroes into southern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/anatolia">Anatolia</a>, and cities of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pamphylia">Pamphylia</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pisidia">Pisidia</a>, such as Perge and Selge, claimed them as founders.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/calchas.jpg" alt="Calchas" width="320" height="480" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: BeakheadIntrados · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Sacrifice_of_Iphigenia,_from_Pompeii_VI.8.3_peristyle._Naples,_Archaeological_Museum_9112_-_07_-_detail_of_Agamemnon.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
